   "text": "A curve $C$ has equation\n$$y = \\frac{\\left(x\\sqrt{x} - 4\\right)^2}{x^3}, \\qquad x > 0.$$\nFind $\\frac{\\mathrm{d}y}{\\mathrm{d}x}$, writing your answer so that every term is a rational constant multiplied by a single power of $x$. Then work out the exact gradient of $C$ where $x = 4$. (4)",
   "mark_scheme": [
    {
     "code": "M1",
     "for": "Expands $(x\\sqrt{x}-4)^2$ and divides each term by $x^3$ to get $y$ as a sum of powers of $x$ (e.g. $1 - 8x^{-\\frac{3}{2}} + 16x^{-3}$, allowing slips in the coefficients), then differentiates, reducing at least one of the powers $-\\tfrac{3}{2}$ or $-3$ by 1",
     "notes": "No marks for applying $nx^{n-1}$ to the numerator and denominator separately. A correct quotient rule attempt on the original fraction also earns M1"
    },
    {
     "code": "A1",
     "for": "One of $12x^{-\\frac{5}{2}}$ or $-48x^{-4}$ correct, simplified or not",
     "depends_on": "M1"
    },
    {
     "code": "A1",
     "for": "$\\frac{\\mathrm{d}y}{\\mathrm{d}x} = 12x^{-\\frac{5}{2}} - 48x^{-4}$ fully correct, with no constant term remaining",
     "depends_on": "M1",
     "notes": "Accept $\\frac{12}{x^{5/2}} - \\frac{48}{x^4}$ oe; isw after a correct answer"
    },
    {
     "code": "B1",
     "for": "Gradient at $x = 4$ is $\\frac{3}{16}$",
     "notes": "cao; accept 0.1875"
    }
   ],
   "solution": [
    {
     "step": 1,
     "working": "$(x\\sqrt{x}-4)^2 = x^3 - 8x^{\\frac{3}{2}} + 16$, so $y = 1 - 8x^{-\\frac{3}{2}} + 16x^{-3}$",
     "mark": "M1 (in part)"
    },
    {
     "step": 2,
     "working": "Differentiate each term: the constant $1$ gives $0$, $-8x^{-\\frac{3}{2}}$ gives $-8\\times(-\\tfrac{3}{2})x^{-\\frac{5}{2}} = 12x^{-\\frac{5}{2}}$",
     "mark": "M1 A1"
    },
    {
     "step": 3,
     "working": "$16x^{-3}$ gives $-48x^{-4}$, so $\\frac{\\mathrm{d}y}{\\mathrm{d}x} = 12x^{-\\frac{5}{2}} - 48x^{-4}$",
     "mark": "A1"
    },
    {
     "step": 4,
     "working": "At $x=4$: $\\frac{12}{4^{5/2}} - \\frac{48}{4^4} = \\frac{12}{32} - \\frac{48}{256} = \\frac{3}{8} - \\frac{3}{16} = \\frac{3}{16}$",
     "mark": "B1"
    }
   ],
